{"name":"Irphong","status":"ok","title":"Irphong","pageId":107475,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\" role=\"region\"><nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Maps_of_Irphong\" title=\"Category:Maps of Irphong\">Gallery</a></nav>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Irphong</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"type\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Island</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Nelanther_Isles\" title=\"Nelanther Isles\">Nelanther Isles</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</aside>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><br/>\nThis lifeless island was used as a marker to show the northern end of <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQXNhdmlyJUUyJTgwJTk5c19DaGFubmVsP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Asavir’s Channel (page does not exist)\">Asavir’s Channel</span>. It's only notable feature is one of the <a href=\"/wiki/Sea_Towers\" title=\"Sea Towers\">Sea Towers</a> was built on the cliff face of the north shore, 150 feet above the sea. Magical light emanates from the tower preventing ships from crashing into the islands or the <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRHJhZ29uJTI3c19IZWFkX1Blbmluc3VsYT9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Dragon's Head Peninsula (page does not exist)\">Dragon's Head Peninsula</span>. <sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-tethyr-p95_1-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-tethyr-p95-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Rumors_.26_Legends\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Rumors_&amp;_Legends\">Rumors &amp; Legends</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Rumors &amp; Legends\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Irphong?veaction=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Rumors &amp; Legends\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>No one willingly approaches the island as it is said that the <a href=\"/wiki/Curse_of_Irphong\" title=\"Curse of Irphong\">Curse of Irphong</a> will find those that do. Whenever a pirate puts down anchor here or even approaches the shoals around it, the ship is cursed to sink within a tenday.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-tethyr-p95_1-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-tethyr-p95-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Irphong?veaction=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Irphong?veaction=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"reflist\" style=\"\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-tethyr-p95-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-tethyr-p95_1-0\">1.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-tethyr-p95_1-1\">1.1</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Steven_E._Schend\" title=\"Steven E. Schend\">Steven E. Schend</a> (August 1997). “Book One: Tethyr”. In <a href=\"/wiki/Roger_E._Moore\" title=\"Roger E. Moore\">Roger E. Moore</a> ed. <i><a href=\"/wiki/Lands_of_Intrigue_(boxed_set)\" title=\"Lands of Intrigue (boxed set)\">Lands of Intrigue</a></i> (<a href=\"/wiki/TSR,_Inc.\" title=\"TSR, Inc.\">TSR, Inc.</a>), p. 95. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-7869-0697-9\" title=\"Special:BookSources/0-7869-0697-9\">0-7869-0697-9</a>.</span>\n</li>\n</ol></div>\n</div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260516182819\nCache expiry: 1209600\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.052 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.065 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 700/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1686/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 792/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 14/100\nExpensive parser function count: 1/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 975/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops count: 0/200\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   52.870      1 -total\n 73.08%   38.640      1 Template:Location\n 19.15%   10.125      1 Template:Refs\n 12.12%    6.409      1 Template:Cite_book/Lands_of_Intrigue/Tethyr\n  9.78%    5.173      1 Template:Cite_book\n  6.96%    3.679      1 Template:Cite_publication\n  2.62%    1.385      2 Template:FormatAlias\n-->\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key 1.43.8_prod_forg